This study examines the Cauchy problem for the Boltzmann equation with moderate collisions, given by \begin{equation} \left\{ \begin{array}{l}
\partial_t f + v \cdot \nabla_x f = Q_\alpha(f,f), \\
f |_{t=0} = f_0, \end{array} \right\} \end{equation} where $Q_\alpha(f,g)$ represents the $\alpha$-truncated Boltzmann collision operator, $0 < \alpha < 1$, and $f$ is a function that depends on time, position, and velocity. We prove the existence and uniqueness of a solution to this problem under small data conditions.
